## Responsive Breakpoints

### Tailwind Breakpoint Reference

- **Mobile (base)**: `< 768px` - Default styles, no prefix
- **Tablet (`md:`)**: `≥ 768px` - Medium screens and up
- **Desktop (`lg:`)**: `≥ 1024px` - Large screens and up

### Breakpoint Usage Pattern

Always use mobile-first approach with responsive prefixes:

```typescript
// Mobile-first: base styles for mobile, then override for larger screens
className="py-8 px-4 md:py-16 md:px-8 lg:py-24 lg:px-12"

// NOT desktop-first
// className="lg:py-24 md:py-16 py-8" // Avoid this pattern
```

## Best Practices

### Do's

- ✅ Always use responsive spacing utilities (`py-8 md:py-16 lg:py-24`)
- ✅ Check background colors before applying adjacent section spacing
- ✅ Use column gaps that match section horizontal padding
- ✅ Apply mobile-first responsive design
- ✅ Use semantic HTML (`<section>` elements)
- ✅ Maintain consistent spacing ratios (2:1 for full:half)
- ✅ Test spacing on all breakpoints
- ✅ Use Tailwind's gap utilities for column spacing
- ✅ Document exceptions when deviating from standards

### Don'ts

- ❌ Don't mix different spacing systems (stick to Tailwind utilities)
- ❌ Don't use adjacent spacing for sections with different backgrounds
- ❌ Don't forget to check background colors before reducing spacing
- ❌ Don't use fixed pixel values - use Tailwind spacing scale
- ❌ Don't skip responsive breakpoints
- ❌ Don't use margins for column spacing (use `gap-*` utilities)
- ❌ Don't apply adjacent spacing to first/last sections unnecessarily
- ❌ Don't mix `gap-*` with manual margins in the same container

## Exceptions and Special Cases

### Hero Sections

Hero sections may use different spacing patterns:
- Full viewport height sections may use `min-h-screen` with centered content
- Hero sections can deviate from standard spacing if design requires it
- Document any hero-specific spacing in component comments

```typescript
// Hero section exception
<section className="min-h-screen flex items-center justify-center py-8 px-4 md:py-16 md:px-8">
  {/* Hero content - may use different spacing */}
</section>
```

### Full-Width Sections

Sections that span full width (no horizontal padding):
- Use `w-full` or container classes
- Still apply vertical padding: `py-8 md:py-16 lg:py-24`
- Remove horizontal padding: `px-0` or omit `px-*` classes

```typescript
// Full-width section
<section className="w-full py-8 md:py-16 lg:py-24">
  {/* Full-width content */}
</section>
```

### Container Sections

Sections with max-width containers:
- Apply section padding to the outer `<section>` element
- Use container classes (`container`, `container mx-auto`) for content width
- Maintain column spacing within containers

```typescript
// Container section
<section className="py-8 px-4 md:py-16 md:px-8 lg:py-24 lg:px-12">
  <div className="container mx-auto">
    <div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 md:gap-8 lg:gap-12">
      {/* Content */}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
```

## Spacing Reference Table

### Section Padding

| Breakpoint | Vertical (py) | Horizontal (px) | Half Vertical |
|------------|----------------|-----------------|---------------|
| Mobile (base) | `py-8` | `px-4` | `py-4` |
| Tablet (md:) | `md:py-16` | `md:px-8` | `md:py-8` |
| Desktop (lg:) | `lg:py-24` | `lg:px-12` | `lg:py-16` |

### Column Gaps

| Breakpoint | Gap Utility |
|------------|-------------|
| Mobile (base) | `gap-4` |
| Tablet (md:) | `md:gap-8` |
| Desktop (lg:) | `lg:gap-12` |

### Adjacent Section Spacing

| Breakpoint | First Section | Second Section |
|------------|---------------|----------------|
| Mobile | `pt-8 pb-4` | `pb-8 pt-4` |
| Tablet | `md:pt-16 md:pb-8` | `md:pb-16 md:pt-8` |
| Desktop | `lg:pt-24 lg:pb-16` | `lg:pb-24 lg:pt-16` |

## Integration with Existing Patterns

### Component Development

When creating new page components:
1. Wrap content in `<section>` elements
2. Apply appropriate spacing classes based on background color context
3. Use column gaps for internal layouts
4. Follow responsive breakpoint patterns

### Layout Integration

Page layouts should:
- Allow sections to control their own spacing
- Not override section spacing at the layout level
- Provide consistent container structure when needed

### Migration Notes

When updating existing pages:
1. Identify sections with same background colors
2. Apply adjacent spacing rules where appropriate
3. Update column layouts to use standard gap utilities
4. Ensure all spacing is responsive
5. Test on all breakpoints
